  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhance sustainability and competitiveness in small and medium-sized enterprises through sustainable circular packaging solutions and standard compliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This initiative consists of an inception phase aimed at preparing a full-scale project that promotes sustainability standards and circular packaging solutions for Guatemalan SMEs in the food sector. By conducting technical assessments of value chains, packaging systems, market access, and quality infrastructure, alongside gender analysis and stakeholder engagement, the phase will deliver a validated project proposal for Phase 2. The initiative seeks to ensure compliance with evolving sustainability regulations, enhance SME competitiveness, promote circular practices, reduce food loss, and strengthen the sector#s access to high-value markets, with funding provided by the Swedish Embassy in Guatemala.</narrative>
  </description>
